111 │ 	/**
112 │ 	 * Every Transfer in every status, newest first, or the one status {@code status} names.
113 │ 	 *
114 │ 	 * <p><b>Every status, which is design decision 19's reading of the requirement rather
115 │ 	 * than a liberty taken with it.</b> The task asks for executed transfers, written against
116 │ 	 * a synchronous model where a Transfer is either done or never existed. Under the
117 │ 	 * asynchronous lifecycle of ADR-0001 a {@code PENDING} Transfer appearing nowhere would
118 │ 	 * make the only list screen actively misleading: an operator would believe their Transfer
119 │ 	 * had vanished. The filter is what narrows it to settled Transfers for a caller who wants
120 │ 	 * that.
121 │ 	 *
122 │ 	 * <p>A bare array rather than an object wrapping one, and a status typed as the enum
123 │ 	 * rather than a string, both on {@code AccountController#listAccounts}'s reasoning: an
124 │ 	 * envelope earns its place when there is something to put beside the items, and design
125 │ 	 * decision 31 declines pagination. A status this domain has no name for is refused by the
126 │ 	 * conversion, and {@code ProblemDocumentAdvice} reports it against {@code status} in the
127 │ 	 * shape a rejected body field gets.
128 │ 	 */
129 │ 	@GetMapping
130 │ 	List<TransferResponse> listTransfers(@RequestParam(required = false) @Nullable TransferStatus status) {
131 │ 		return transfers.list(status).stream().map(TransferResponse::of).toList();
132 │ 	}
133 │ 
134 │ 	/**
135 │ 	 * One Transfer, at the URL the {@code 201} above points at. This is the resource that lets
136 │ 	 * a pending Transfer's state live in the URL rather than in the tab that submitted it, so
137 │ 	 * a refresh shows where the Transfer has got to instead of losing it.
138 │ 	 *
139 │ 	 * <p>The same {@link TransferResponse} the listing sends, member for member. Ticket 22
140 │ 	 * adds the Check Ledger to this response and to this one only — what a Transfer is waiting
141 │ 	 * on is what a single Transfer is fetched to find out, and it is not a column.
142 │ 	 */
143 │ 	@GetMapping("/{id}")
144 │ 	TransferResponse fetchTransfer(@PathVariable long id) {
145 │ 		return TransferResponse.of(transfers.byId(id));
146 │ 	}
